{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-07-10T09:45:36.639Z","sessionId":"96450f51-d651-4f84-a2b8-70f86383cafe","content":"gemini created the following for accessing space agent benny from my kindle and making it accessible through a web browser UI, I liked the rekindle app and the layout, review the requirement and implementation and what you think might be a better features and interactions, give me a back a prompt to tell Anitgravity how to improve it ReKindle × Space Agent — Walkthrough\nWhat Was Built\nA self-hosted ReKindle fork that provides a simplified, e-ink-friendly alternative interface for the Space Agent application, fully integrated with the Benny AI backend.\nArchitecture\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│           site/rekindle/  (static HTML/JS/CSS)   │\n│                                                   │\n│  index.html ─── Home dashboard with app grid      │\n│  files.html ─── File browser → Space Agent API    │\n│  reader.html ── EPUB/PDF/Markdown reader          │\n│  editor.html ── Markdown edit & preview           │\n│  chat.html ──── Benny AI chat                     │\n│  terminal.html  Log tail viewer (SSE)             │\n│  settings.html  Connection & display settings     │\n│  space-bridge.js  API client (replaces Firebase)  │\n│  css/rekindle.css  E-ink optimized styles         │\n└────────────┬────────────────────┬────────────────┘\n             │                    │\n    ┌────────▼────────┐  ┌───────▼────────┐\n    │  Space Agent    │  │  Benny API     │\n    │  /reader/*      │  │  :8005         │\n    │  /api/file_*    │  │  /api/chat     │\n    │  /api/login_*   │  │  /api/files    │\n    │                 │  │  /api/live     │\n    └─────────────────┘  └────────────────┘\nChanges Made\nNew Files (10)\nFile\tSize\tPurpose\nrekindle.css\n8.4 KB\tE-ink optimized CSS — System 7 aesthetic, no animations, high contrast, dark mode, 44px touch targets\nspace-bridge.js\n11.6 KB\tAPI client replacing Firebase SDK with calls to Space Agent (auth, files) and Benny (chat, RAG, logs, PDF)\nindex.html\n3.3 KB\tHome dashboard with app grid and dual-backend health check\nfiles.html\n7.2 KB\tFile browser connected to Space Agent file_list/file_read with offline caching\nreader.html\n9.4 KB\tUnified reader: PDF (pdf.js + server fallback), Markdown (marked.js), EPUB (placeholder)\neditor.html\n8.0 KB\tMarkdown editor with edit/preview toggle, dirty tracking, auto-save drafts, Ctrl+S\nchat.html\n6.6 KB\tBenny AI chat with markdown rendering, source citations, persistent history (50 messages)\nterminal.html\n5.8 KB\tLog tail viewer with SSE streaming, 3 source tabs (Benny/Space/Longview), pause/download\nsettings.html\n8.2 KB\tConnection settings, connection test, display prefs, data management\nModified Files (3)\nfile_routes.py\nAdded POST /api/files/pdf-extract endpoint:\nExtracts text from PDF files page-by-page using PyMuPDF (fitz)\nFalls back to pdfminer.six if fitz is unavailable\nReturns { title, total_pages, pages: [{ page, text }] }\nEnables legacy e-ink devices to read PDFs as plain text\nlive_routes.py\nAdded GET /api/live/logs SSE endpoint:\nStreams log lines from configurable log files (benny, space, longview)\nResolves log paths from env vars (BENNY_LOG_FILE, etc.) or default locations\nAuto-classifies severity (error/warn/success/info) for terminal UI\nHandles file rotation/truncation gracefully\nFalls back to synthetic status messages when no log file exists\nrouter.js\nAdded /reader/* static file handler:\nServes site/rekindle/ files with correct MIME types\nPlaced just before the page-shell fallback in routing order\nNo auth required (public route for LAN e-ink devices)\nPath traversal prevention\nno-store cache headers for fresh content on reload\nHow To Test\nStart Space Agent: npm run dev or node space serve\nOpen in browser: Navigate to http://localhost:PORT/reader\nLAN e-ink device: Open http://<your-ip>:PORT/reader from a Kindle/Kobo browser\nConfigure backends: Use Settings page to set Space Agent and Benny API URLs\nTest connection: Settings → \"Test Connection\" button checks both backends\nKey Design Decisions\nNo build step: Pure HTML/CSS/JS files, no bundler, no framework — matches ReKindle's philosophy\nDual-backend bridge: space-bridge.js abstracts the fact that two servers exist behind one clean API\nOffline-first: All pages cache data to localStorage with configurable TTLs\nE-ink optimized: Zero animations, high contrast, minimum 44px touch targets, dark mode via prefers-color-scheme\nPublic route: /reader/* requires no auth so any device on the LAN can access the UI directly (API calls still require auth via session cookie)"}
