dle Scribe; same-origin /api/runtime auth fix + pen→VIS-001 ingest direction; improvement plan handed to Antigravity\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 96450f51-d651-4f84-a2b8-70f86383cafe\n---\n\nGemini/Antigravity built a self-hosted ReKindle fork at `prime-silo/site/rekindle/`\n(static HTML/JS/CSS, no build) giving the **Kindle Scribe** an e-ink browser UI over\nSpace Agent + Benny. Files: index/files/reader/editor/chat/terminal/settings.html +\n`space-bridge.js` (two-backend API client) + `css/rekindle.css`. Served at `/reader/*`\n(public route in `server/router/router.js` ~L442). I reviewed it and wrote the grounded\nimprovement plan + Antigravity prompt to `prime-silo/site/rekindle/IMPROVEMENTS.md`.\n\n**Target is Kindle Scribe** (modern Chromium e-ink, buttonless, touch+pen) — so ES\nmodules/fetch/async work; the legacy-browser/ES5 concern is moot. Real issues that\nremain: CDN deps (marked/pdf.js) fail on a LAN Scribe with no internet → **vendor\nlocally**; `prefers-color-scheme: dark` is wrong for e-ink; 30s health poll churns the\nscreen; `chat.html:96-99` builds RAG `sourceText` then never renders it (dead code =\nlost citations); reader markdown/text is infinite-scroll (should tap-zone paginate like\nthe PDF path); no reading-position memory.\n\n**Auth fix (turnkey, NO server code):** two systems — Space Agent = session cookie,\nBenny(:8005) = `X-Benny-API-Key` header. A same-origin key-injecting proxy ALREADY\nexists: `router.js` routes `/api/runtime/<path>` → `proxyToRuntime`\n(`server/lib/runtime_proxy.js`), injecting the trusted Benny key server-side →\n`127.0.0.1:8005/api/<path>`. So change `space-bridge.js` ONLY: rewrite Benny calls'\nleading `/api/`→`/api/runtime/`, base on same-origin `spaceUrl` with\n`credentials:'include'`, delete the client-side key header → Benny key never touches the\ndevice. (Residual same-origin gap in that proxy is documented + fine for personal LAN.)\n\n**Strategic direction — pen → PDF → vision ingest.** Goal: handwrite notes on\nmulti-page/varied-layout docs on the Scribe → annotated PDF → structured knowledge. The\ningest half already exists (this is [[project_prime_silo_vision_ingestion]] / VIS-001):\n`POST /api/vision/docmodel` → `/api/vision/enrich` (enriched markdown into `data_in/`) →\n`/api/rag/ingest`. Phase 1 (ship first): one-tap \"Ingest this PDF\" using the Scribe's\nNATIVE markup export (real low-latency ink the browser can't match). Phase 2 (prototype\nfirst): in-browser inking with vendored pdf.js + pdf-lib. **Unproven assumption to\ntest:** that the enrich describer actually reads HANDWRITING, not just printed text.\n\nRelated: [[project_binary16_app_registry]], [[benny_pilot_documents_and_no_selection_fix]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":40,"oldLines":4,"newStart":40,"newLines":17,"lines":[" first): in-browser inking with vendored pdf.js + pdf-lib. **Unproven assumption to"," test:** that the enrich describer actually reads HANDWRITING, not just printed text."," ","-Related: [[project_binary16_app_registry]], [[benny_pilot_documents_and_no_selection_fix]].","+**Portal expansion (2026-07-11):** ReKindle is now scoped as the Binary16 Labs","+**portal/remote** (IMPROVEMENTS.md Steps 7-8). Graphs-on-e-ink solved by the proven","+LONGVIEW dashboard pattern (`scratch/longview_run/dashboard/` — inline hand-drawn SVG,","+no libs, precomputed dashboard.json, works on Kindle; serve.mjs binds 0.0.0.0:8788 —","+fold under portal origin, don't keep a second unauth origin). Device tiers: lite","+(e-ink: static SVG, tap-to-drill, no animation) vs full (link to real Space Agent);","+capability-probe + manual override. Remote control principle: ADR-001 blocks AGENTS,","+not an authenticated HUMAN on the /api/runtime facade — so Kindle control is in-bounds","+via a fixed allowlisted action registry (no arbitrary shell), session-authed, audited,","+two-tap confirm. Registry v1 (needs user confirmation): LONGVIEW collector/phases,","+ingest-PDF