rd's static files same-origin and drop the second listener) so the tile ships this pass. Port to a native ReKindle page (b) only when a second consumer of `/api/runtime` data appears — don't rewrite a working page for purity. One requirement on (a): once proxied, lock `serve.mjs` back to `DASH_HOST=127.0.0.1` so the unauthenticated `0.0.0.0:8788` origin disappears.\n\n**Step 8 — yes, framework + one PoC action, then pause.** \"Start LONGVIEW collector\" is the right PoC — it's read-only on run state (per `dash.sh`'s own header comment), so a stray fire is harmless. The pause-for-review deliverable is: the registry mechanism, the audit log entry, the 401-when-unauthenticated proof, and the *proposed* full registry as a list for sign-off. Nothing else wired.\n\n**Ordering — 1–5 first, verified on the Scribe, then stop.** They're the correctness blockers and every later step rides Step 5's auth. Ship them as one pass with on-device evidence (LAN-only network, no CDN, same-origin `/api/runtime/*` calls, no key on device). Then 6–8 as a second pass — they're independent of each other, so within that pass order by value: **7a (dashboard tile) → 6 (ingest) → 8 (PoC)**. 7a is nearly free, 6 is the strategic feature, 8 ends exactly at the review gate anyway.\n\nOne thing to hold Antigravity to across all of this: **every \"verified\" claim needs on-device evidence, not desktop-Chrome evidence.** That's the standard failure mode in this project's history — \"e-ink optimized\" was already claimed once without a device test."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":706,"cache_read_input_tokens":112166,"output_tokens":2040,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":706,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2040,"cache_read_input_t